NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The bare minimum to get started with TanStack Form is to create a form and add a field. Keep in mind that this example does not include any validation or error handling... yet."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createForm } from '@tanstack/solid-form'\n\nfunction App() {\n  const form = createForm(() => ({\n    defaultValues: {\n      fullName: '',\n    },\n    onSubmit: async ({ value }) => {\n      // Do something with form data\n      console.log(value)\n    },\n  }))\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>Simple Form Example</h1>\n      <form\n        onSubmit={(e) => {\n          e.preventDefault()\n          e.stopPropagation()\n          form.handleSubmit()\n        }}\n      >\n        <div>\n          <form.Field\n            name=\"fullName\"\n            children={(field) => (\n              <input\n                name={field().name}\n                value={field().state.value}\n                onBlur={field().handleBlur}\n                onInput={(e) => field().handleChange(e.target.value)}\n              />\n            )}\n          />\n        </div>\n        <button type=\"submit\">Submit</button>\n      </form>\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"From here, you'll be ready to explore all of the other features of TanStack Form!"}]}],"headings":[]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe bare minimum to get started with TanStack Form is to create a form and add a field. Keep in mind that this example does not include any validation or error handling... yet.\n\n```tsx\nimport { createForm } from '@tanstack/solid-form'\n\nfunction App() {\n  const form = createForm(() => ({\n    defaultValues: {\n      fullName: '',\n    },\n    onSubmit: async ({ value }) => {\n      // Do something with form data\n      console.log(value)\n    },\n  }))\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>Simple Form Example</h1>\n      <form\n        onSubmit={(e) => {\n          e.preventDefault()\n          e.stopPropagation()\n          form.handleSubmit()\n        }}\n      >\n        <div>\n          <form.Field\n            name=\"fullName\"\n            children={(field) => (\n              <input\n                name={field().name}\n                value={field().state.value}\n                onBlur={field().handleBlur}\n                onInput={(e) => field().handleChange(e.target.value)}\n              />\n            )}\n          />\n        </div>\n        <button type=\"submit\">Submit</button>\n      </form>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nFrom here, you'll be ready to explore all of the other features of TanStack Form!\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: quick-start\ntitle: Quick Start\n---\n\nThe bare minimum to get started with TanStack Form is to create a form and add a field. Keep in mind that this example does not include any validation or error handling... yet.\n\n```tsx\nimport { createForm } from '@tanstack/solid-form'\n\nfunction App() {\n  const form = createForm(() => ({\n    defaultValues: {\n      fullName: '',\n    },\n    onSubmit: async ({ value }) => {\n      // Do something with form data\n      console.log(value)\n    },\n  }))\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>Simple Form Example</h1>\n      <form\n        onSubmit={(e) => {\n          e.preventDefault()\n          e.stopPropagation()\n          form.handleSubmit()\n        }}\n      >\n        <div>\n          <form.Field\n            name=\"fullName\"\n            children={(field) => (\n              <input\n                name={field().name}\n                value={field().state.value}\n                onBlur={field().handleBlur}\n                onInput={(e) => field().handleChange(e.target.value)}\n              />\n            )}\n          />\n        </div>\n        <button type=\"submit\">Submit</button>\n      </form>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nFrom here, you'll be ready to explore all of the other features of TanStack Form!\n"}
